course: dictionary
lesson: 6218
title: Misty
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Misty is an adjective, and it has more than one meaning. The first meaning is about weather: misty means full of mist, so it is hard to see far. «On a misty autumn morning the garden is full of spider webs shining with dew.» The clues are morning, dew and the word full, so misty means the air is full of mist.
explain: Mist is made of tiny water drops in the air. It is thinner than fog, so you can often still see a little way through it. Because you cannot see clearly, people use care: on misty mornings, drivers and cyclists turn on their lights so others can see them.
explain: Misty can also describe eyes or memories. «Her eyes were misty as she waved goodbye» means her eyes were full of tears. «I have a misty memory of that day» means the memory is unclear, not sharp. Always check the clues around the word to see which meaning fits.
fact: Misty means full of mist, so it is hard to see far.
fact: Mist is tiny water drops in the air, and it is thinner than fog.
fact: «Misty eyes» are eyes full of tears.
fact: A «misty memory» is one that is unclear, not sharp.
fact: Misty, mistier and mistiest show how mist can grow more or less: a morning can be a bit misty, very misty, or the most misty of all.
exercise: «On a misty autumn morning the garden is full of spider webs shining with dew.» What does misty mean here? | Full of loud birds | *Full of mist, so it is hard to see far | Cold and icy | Shiny like glass
exercise: «Her eyes were misty as she waved goodbye.» What does misty mean in this sentence? | *Full of tears | Dusty | Sleepy | Shut tight
exercise: «In autumn the Great Square of Pegasus climbs in the east, and from its corner a line of stars leads to the misty smudge of the Andromeda Galaxy.» Find and copy the word that tells you the smudge is hard to see clearly. | line | corner | *misty | climbs
test: In weather, what is mist? | A hot wind from the desert | Smoke from a bonfire | *Tiny water drops in the air, thinner than fog | Dust blown up by the wind
test: Why do drivers and cyclists use lights on misty mornings? | To keep the bicycle warm | *So that other people can see them more easily | Because it is always night | To make the mist go away
exam: Dad says, «I have a misty memory of that day.» What does misty mean? | Full of tears | *Unclear, hard to remember clearly | Very cold | Shining bright
